<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xianyang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xianyang is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi'an</a>. It was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> from 350 BCE and then of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a>, where the First Emperor built vast palaces. It was burned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> in 206 BCE, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> built its new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xianyang.jpg" alt="Xianyang" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brücke-Osteuropa · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maoling_10.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
